WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.350
with South America

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:20.720
[Music]

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.660
flying over New York it is easy to understand
why there are so many tall buildings on the

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:31.220
small island of Manhattan here the only way
that enough room can be made for business

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:41.210
places and homes is to erect higher and higher
buildings many of these are called skyscrapers

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:47.140
the Metropolis of New York is actually made
up of several large cities the most important

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:53.210
of these cities within the city is the crowded
island of Manhattan where two million people

00:00:53.210 --> 00:01:00.630
live another 3 million live elsewhere but
have jobs in Manhattan and every day hundreds

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:05.830
of thousands come to the city as visitors

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:11.710
in a crowded Metropolis like New York people
have difficulty in finding places to live

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:19.960
Park Avenue the city's best known residential
street is lined with tall apartment houses

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:25.549
another section of Manhattan has the largest
negro population of any community in the world

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:33.140
this is Harlem

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:38.820
in much of Harlem as in other parts of New
York families live crowded together in tenement

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.600
houses

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.440
some sections of New York such as the one
called Little Italy seem almost like communities

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.550
in a foreign land these neighborhoods were
settled by immigrants who arrived in New York

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:57.299
from countries in the old world others who
came later found life in the new world less

00:01:57.299 --> 00:02:03.710
strange by living with those who could speak
their own language in Chinatown most of the

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:09.050
residents are people whose parents or grandparents
came to the United States from the far away

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:14.959
Orient

00:02:14.959 --> 00:02:20.590
many different races and nationalities make
up the population of New York this Metropolis

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:25.800
has been called a melting pot because sooner
or later its people become Americans

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:37.500
in some parts of the city worn out tenements
are being replaced by groups of modern skyscraper

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:44.530
homes in these buildings hundreds of families
have their own separate sets of rooms called

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:50.019
housekeeping Apartments the crowded island
of Manhattan is but one of the five divisions

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:56.430
of New York City these divisions are called
Burrows besides Manhattan there are the Bronx

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:03.120
Queens Brooklyn and Richmond and for Miles
beyond the activities of the people are so

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:10.060
closely linked with New York that the entire
area is known as greater New York

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:16.120
a New York family wishing to occupy a single
house with even a small lawn or garden must

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:21.130
live miles away from the business district
communities surrounding the city are called

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:27.230
suburbs although in the suburbs of New York
homes are built close together families enjoy

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:31.019
more freedom and are not troubled by the noise
of the big city

00:03:31.019 --> 00:03:38.959
the transportation of the millions of people
who go back and forth to Manhattan Island

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:44.709
every working day is a tremendous problem
people who do business in the city but live

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:50.480
in the suburbs are called commuters a great
many of these people make their daily trips

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.870
by train

00:03:53.870 --> 00:04:00.810
morning and evening rush hours all means of
transportation are crowded with passengers

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:06.670
ferry boats run back and forth across the
rivers and Bays that surround Manhattan Island

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.439
most people who travel by ferry come from
communities in New Jersey and in the borough

00:04:11.439 --> 00:04:15.540
of Richmond

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:20.430
before Bridges were built to link Manhattan
with the mainland ferry boats were the only

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:29.160
means of moving passengers and vehicles to
the island

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:42.640
today New York has the most elaborate rapid
transit system of any city in the world thank

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:51.320
you

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:56.870
because there is no longer room for tracks
above ground trains go underground into Subways

00:04:56.870 --> 00:05:03.169
and tunnels as they approach the crowded areas
of the city tunnels have been bored deep under

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:08.550
the rivers and fast electric trains run on
tracks laid beneath streets and buildings

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:17.699
these underground Railways make it possible
for New Yorkers to get about the city quickly

00:05:17.699 --> 00:05:22.680
moving stairs help passengers from the subway
stations far below ground to the level of

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:28.229
the streets

00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:32.960
because Manhattan is an island a great many
bridges are needed so that Automobiles and

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.199
trucks can go in and out of the city

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:43.080
the George Washington Bridge spans the Hudson
River and connects the highways of New Jersey

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:58.319
with Express highways that run around the
island of Manhattan

00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:04.200
New York's Express Highway is also connect
with tunnels constructed just for motor traffic

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:09.270
four great highways built under the rivers
lead from various parts of the Island to New

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:14.789
Jersey Brooklyn and Queens

00:06:14.789 --> 00:06:20.860
these tunnels are used by Passenger cars buses
and by The Fleets of trucks which haul goods

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.650
and supplies for the minions who live in the
city

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:37.349
[Music] tons and tons of food are needed every
day for homes restaurants and hotels because

00:06:37.349 --> 00:06:42.690
the land on Manhattan Island is too valuable
to be used for raising food everything in

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:50.310
the market comes from outside the city Farms
as far away as Oregon California and Texas

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:56.360
help feed the minions who live in the Metropolis

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:00.879
because there is little space for storage
in Manhattan Fresh Foods must be delivered

00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:03.169
to Big Central Markets every day

00:07:03.169 --> 00:07:10.259
okay

00:07:10.259 --> 00:07:15.419
during the early morning hours produce from
all over the country has distributed to thousands

00:07:15.419 --> 00:07:28.080
of smaller markets grocery stores and restaurants

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:33.660
at noon time streets are filled with lunch
hour crowds throughout New York's business

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:40.580
districts there are restaurants to suit every
taste and every pocketbook automats are cafeterias

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:45.970
where customers drop coins in a slot and in
return obtain food quickly

00:07:45.970 --> 00:08:02.419
[Music] grouped around one short and Narrow
Street at the lower end of Manhattan are many

00:08:02.419 --> 00:08:08.550
big Banks and investment firms the money that
comes to Wall Street belongs to millions of

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:14.360
people everywhere who have put their Savings
in bank accounts insurance policies stocks

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:21.650
and bonds these Financial companies provide
much of the money needed to carry on business

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:30.569
and to expand industry in the United States
as well as abroad

00:08:30.569 --> 00:08:35.229
the money to build skyscrapers comes from
Wall Street firms that make a business of

00:08:35.229 --> 00:08:40.419
investing money for other people the Empire
State Building cost many millions of dollars

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:48.300
to build and is the tallest structure in the
entire world this skyscraper is 102 stories

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:54.500
from top to bottom it provides New York's
crowded Midtown area with space for thousands

00:08:54.500 --> 00:09:00.420
of additional offices and shops yet it occupies
less than one block of the city's valuable

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:01.420
land

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:10.580
the Chrysler Building has 77 stories and like
other skyscrapers provides headquarters for

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:16.620
big businesses that have offices all over
the country

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:21.190
the group of tall buildings at Rockefeller
Center is almost like another city within

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:27.459
the Metropolis

00:09:27.459 --> 00:09:33.149
many of these buildings are occupied by radio
and television Studios advertising agencies

00:09:33.149 --> 00:09:38.750
and insurance companies which serve the entire
nation people like these earn their living

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:49.839
by doing things which other people want instead
of making things

00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:54.230
hundreds of people work for press associations
upon which newspapers all over the country

00:09:54.230 --> 00:10:03.740
depend

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:09.910
but within the Metropolis of New York a great
variety of goods is manufactured the largest

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:16.260
industry is the making of all kinds of clothes
from underwear to fur coats more than a third

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:25.570
of all the clothing worn in the United States
is made in Manhattan's Midtown garment Center

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:30.120
this industry developed in New York chiefly
because great numbers of garment workers came

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:37.690
here from Europe

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:44.560
with them came dress designers and the city
soon became a Fashion Center the manufacturer

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:50.010
of a single garment may be done in several
different workshops in this heavily congested

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:55.510
District it is cheaper and faster to move
clothing from one shop to another in hand

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:56.510
carts

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:08.600
foreign

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:13.149
stores all over the country sell clothing
patterned after Styles seen in Manhattan's

00:11:13.149 --> 00:11:21.399
most expensive shops New York like every Metropolis
is a great trading center upper Fifth Avenue

00:11:21.399 --> 00:11:27.500
shopping district is the most fashionable
in the country many new styles are first shown

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:29.190
in Fifth Avenue stores

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:36.460
[Music]

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:43.740
[Applause]

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:48.890
the window displays of shops along 5th Avenue
are one of the principal attractions for most

00:11:48.890 --> 00:12:00.130
visitors to New York

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:05.540
many dealers import expensive merchandise
from abroad While others specialize in fine

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:14.980
American-made products

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:20.490
whatever the world makes to sell can be purchased
in New York even the rarest of luxuries may

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:28.000
find a buyer among the minions who shop in
the city all right

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:34.500
[Music] just as the Metropolis of New York
is a center of Transportation industry and

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:41.829
trade it is also a great cultural center of
all its many museums and art galleries none

00:12:41.829 --> 00:12:52.940
is more famous than the Metropolitan Museum
of Art

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:59.140
almost every day classes from some public
or private school visit the Metropolitan admission

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:05.199
to the museum is free of charge a great many
students attend art schools in New York in

00:13:05.199 --> 00:13:18.300
order to make use of the city's many museums

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:23.820
The Collection owned by the Metropolitan is
one of the largest in the world it is a National

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:39.540
Treasure whose worth cannot be measured

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:44.910
it is almost a miracle that in the very heart
of crowded Manhattan Island an immense tract

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.480
of land has been reserved for a public park

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:56.050
come back

00:13:56.050 --> 00:14:05.490
[Music] The Men Who planned for New York's
growth had great vision long ago they foresaw

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:11.540
the need for Central Park Manhattan's great
outdoor playground where the city's minions

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:15.420
now enjoy grassy spaces and the cool shade
of trees

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:20.889
[Music]

00:14:20.889 --> 00:14:40.740
thank you [Music] but millions of New York
families live too far away from the city's

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:46.279
parks and playgrounds to visit them every
day the children whose homes are in crowded

00:14:46.279 --> 00:14:59.190
neighborhoods have no choice but to make playgrounds
out of the streets

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:04.950
on hot summer days an opened fire hydrant
is the city child substitute for waiting in

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:12.149
a Cool Running Brook

00:15:12.149 --> 00:15:29.190
and for older boys the swimming hole is at
the end of one of the city's hundreds of Piers

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:35.500
Coney Island one of New York's largest beaches
faces the Atlantic Ocean and is easily reached

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:41.540
by subway trains throughout the summer months
Coney Island is crowded with people seeking

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:48.360
relief from the sweltering heat of the city

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:54.199
at night the brightest reflection in the Skies
over New York comes from Manhattan the biggest

00:15:54.199 --> 00:15:59.790
entertainment center in the world is the area
around Times Square and Broadway the great

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:05.579
white way within walking distance of Times
Square there are hundreds of theaters stage

00:16:05.579 --> 00:16:14.130
plays and motion pictures here too of the
Opera the ballet and concerts

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:20.860
a metropolis is more than just one big city
it is a city made up of many cities that serves

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:26.740
not only its own people but also the nation
it is a great Center of Transportation industry

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:31.690
and trade where millions of people live and
work and play

